    {
      "id": 22540,
      "name": "awp832",
      "username": "awp832",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-12-23T08:46:44.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If you think Visionary is the weakest hero, you should try to play her some more. &nbsp; I think she's one of the strongest. &nbsp;Of course you can play how you want, but the nerf to wrest the mind was very much needed and balances her nicely. &nbsp;<em>Suggestion &nbsp;</em>in particular is profoundly strong. &nbsp;<em>Mental Divergence&nbsp;</em>is also an amazing card, whose only real drawback is that you can't really use it and <em>Enlighten</em> at the same time (without aid from another hero of course). &nbsp; <em>Enlighten</em> is one of the best support powers in the base game, second to <em>Galvanize</em> and that's all. &nbsp;And of course, <em>Wrest the Mind&nbsp;</em>is very strong, slap it on a powerful card, electroupulse explosive, Voss' dreadnaughts, T-rexes, Krakens, &nbsp;whatever. &nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:56:34.919Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
