      "id": 22542,
      "name": "Reckless",
      "username": "Reckless",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-12-23T18:35:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"bandbc\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bandbc/48/2842_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bandbc:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In my opinon, we will not play by this Errata. The Visionary is the weakest of the Heros in the first place, and this is the one card that balences her out in play. I think you need to leave this one alone. Just my opinon.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Errata-free Wrest the Mind supercombo:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Visionary plays Wrest the Mind on herself.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Any damage she deals to herself is redirected.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>3.&nbsp; When she deals damage, she deals two more damage and then two to herself (which is redirected and causes her to deal even more damage).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This is broken.&nbsp; Without the errata this is pretty much an auto-win.&nbsp; My group thought The Visionary wasn't very good at first.&nbsp; Then we played Wrest the Mind (with errata) on an Electro-Pulse Explosive and utterly destroyed it and Omnitron.&nbsp; If I were you, I would play with the errata before arguing whether it throws her out of balance or not.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:56:35.069Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
